        <activityName xml:lang="en">Concentrated lithium brine (6.7 %  Li), at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Concentrated lithium brine (6.7 %  Li), at plant
Concentrated lithium brine is base material for lithium carbonate.;
CAS number: 000554-13-2; 
UUID: a4e2edac-6522-39d1-8091-6f62428c6a0f
This dataset includes the inspissation of lithium containing brine to a concentrated lithium brine by sun energy in the desert of Atacama (Chile)
Location: Production site is in Chile, all data originate from an environmental survey about the plant in Chile. This dataset can be used globally, as this plant produces 70% of the Li2CO3 worldwide. Brasil electricity mix is used as proxy.
Technology: The inspissation of the brine takes place in the desert of Atacama. The required energy for the inspissation is provided by the sun.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: ecoinvental survey 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty is assessed using the pedigree matrix.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a4e2edac-6522-39d1-8091-6f62428c6a0f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
